{"nodes": [{"id": "extracted_projects_the_method_findings_lowdin_2_13_lowdin_challenge", "label": "The Lowdin Challenge", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "extracted/projects/the-method/FINDINGS-LOWDIN-2_13.txt", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Lowdin asked in 1969 for a derivation of the n+l filling rule from the Schrodinger equation; it has stood since."}, {"id": "extracted_projects_the_method_findings_lowdin_2_13_chapter_lowdin", "label": "CHAPTER-LOWDIN - Draft, Unfinished and Deliberately So", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "extracted/projects/the-method/FINDINGS-LOWDIN-2_13.txt", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Supersedes section 34 of The Method 1.6, which still presents nu as the solution; every claim carries its register number."}, {"id": "extracted_projects_the_method_findings_lowdin_2_13_madelung_wrong_target", "label": "The n+l Rule Is Not What Atoms Obey", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "extracted/projects/the-method/FINDINGS-LOWDIN-2_13.txt", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Madelung inverts 5d/4f and 6d/5f; seventeen of nineteen openings agree and two do not, so deriving n+l exactly would mean deriving something false at two elements."}, {"id": "extracted_projects_the_method_findings_lowdin_2_13_nu_ordering_functional", "label": "nu(n, l, q) - The Ordering Functional", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "extracted/projects/the-method/FINDINGS-LOWDIN-2_13.txt", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Both Pauli quantities appear: the capacity governs admissibility and also sits inside the radicand counting the states below."}, {"id": "extracted_projects_the_method_findings_lowdin_2_13_nu_deactivation", "label": "nu Deactivated as a Law, Retained as a Form", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "extracted/projects/the-method/FINDINGS-LOWDIN-2_13.txt", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Three independent findings force it: the score was fitted, the physical reading is structurally impossible, and register 1303 already knew."}, {"id": "extracted_projects_the_method_findings_lowdin_2_13_held_out_score", "label": "The Held-Out Score - 90 Against Madelung's 96", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "extracted/projects/the-method/FINDINGS-LOWDIN-2_13.txt", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A construction that loses to the rule it was built to explain has not explained it; the placement using the least information wins, which is an overfitting signature."}, {"id": "extracted_projects_the_method_findings_lowdin_2_13_additive_representability", "label": "The Corridor Is Additive Representability", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "extracted/projects/the-method/FINDINGS-LOWDIN-2_13.txt", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Kraft-Pratt-Seidenberg 1959, Scott 1964, Krantz-Luce-Suppes-Tversky 1971; empty feasible sets correspond exactly to cancellation conditions."}, {"id": "extracted_projects_the_method_findings_lowdin_2_13_fishburn_warning", "label": "Fishburn's Standing Warning", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "extracted/projects/the-method/FINDINGS-LOWDIN-2_13.txt", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Feasibility checked at low order is not representability; any future corridor must be solved as a system rather than spot-checked."}, {"id": "extracted_projects_the_method_findings_lowdin_2_13_helly_number", "label": "Helly's Number h = d + 1, Three Names for One Number", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "extracted/projects/the-method/FINDINGS-LOWDIN-2_13.txt", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Register 489's 'one level short', Freuder's k-consistency and the KPS cancellation conditions are three names for h."}, {"id": "extracted_projects_the_method_findings_lowdin_2_13_conflict_graph", "label": "The Conflict Graph and the Maximum Clique as Verdict", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "extracted/projects/the-method/FINDINGS-LOWDIN-2_13.txt", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Vertices are constraints, an edge joins two that cannot hold together; Lambda has clique 1 and closes, the nuclear corridor clique 2 and is refuted, Lowdin clique 3."}, {"id": "extracted_projects_the_method_findings_lowdin_2_13_nuclear_corridor_rank_one", "label": "The Nuclear Corridor's Rank-One Certificate", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "extracted/projects/the-method/FINDINGS-LOWDIN-2_13.txt", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Six constraint vectors are all positive multiples of (4, 1), giving a second-order cancellation - the shortest such a system can have."}, {"id": "extracted_projects_the_method_findings_lowdin_2_13_demkov_ostrovsky_potential", "label": "Demkov-Ostrovsky Focusing Potential (1971/72)", "file_type": "paper", "source_file": "extracted/projects/the-method/FINDINGS-LOWDIN-2_13.txt", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "U(r) proportional to -r^-1 (r+R)^-2 produces additional degeneracy for levels with identical N = n+l at energy E = 0."}, {"id": "extracted_projects_the_method_findings_lowdin_2_13_guessed_potential_objection", "label": "The Guessed-Potential Objection", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "extracted/projects/the-method/FINDINGS-LOWDIN-2_13.txt", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Thyssen and Ceulemans: correct results obtained from a guessed effective potential cannot count as a solution; the objection applies with equal force to nu."}, {"id": "extracted_projects_the_method_findings_lowdin_2_13_belokolos", "label": "Belokolos (2017)", "file_type": "paper", "source_file": "extracted/projects/the-method/FINDINGS-LOWDIN-2_13.txt", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Derives Madelung's first rule by requiring Coulomb behaviour at the origin; answers the guessed-potential objection but ranks 87 of 106 and answers a different question."}, {"id": "extracted_projects_the_method_findings_lowdin_2_13_kholodenko_kauffman", "label": "Kholodenko and Kauffman (2019, 2020)", "file_type": "paper", "source_file": "extracted/projects/the-method/FINDINGS-LOWDIN-2_13.txt", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Modified Bertrand theorem and Tietz-type equations; claims an analytic solution but concedes the Madelung exceptions are not described in detail."}, {"id": "extracted_projects_the_method_findings_lowdin_2_13_allen_knight", "label": "Allen and Knight (2002/2003)", "file_type": "paper", "source_file": "extracted/projects/the-method/FINDINGS-LOWDIN-2_13.txt", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "An s/p framework internally perturbed by d and f electrons, verified against Desclaux 1973; Scerri's 2006 commentary concludes it is inadequate."}, {"id": "extracted_projects_the_method_findings_lowdin_2_13_tangour_k", "label": "Tangour's Descriptor K(ZX) (2015)", "file_type": "paper", "source_file": "extracted/projects/the-method/FINDINGS-LOWDIN-2_13.txt", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Built from all four quantum numbers of the most recently added electron, claiming no exceptions remain; closest in spirit to putting occupancy inside the ordering functional."}, {"id": "extracted_projects_the_method_findings_lowdin_2_13_schwarz_objection", "label": "Schwarz's Dissenting Position", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "extracted/projects/the-method/FINDINGS-LOWDIN-2_13.txt", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The Madelung rule does not reflect the order of occupation as believed, and usually fails where d and f orbitals are involved - which is exactly where this work's misses fall."}, {"id": "extracted_projects_the_method_findings_lowdin_2_13_scerri_consensus", "label": "Scerri's Statement of the Field's Consensus", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "extracted/projects/the-method/FINDINGS-LOWDIN-2_13.txt", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Numerous authors claim to have met the challenge; the generally held opinion is that none has succeeded as Lowdin intended."}, {"id": "extracted_projects_the_method_findings_lowdin_2_13_out_of_sample_test", "label": "The Out-of-Sample Test Against a Madelung Null", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "extracted/projects/the-method/FINDINGS-LOWDIN-2_13.txt", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "No source in the literature reports one; it converts the challenge from a yes/no into a distance, and on it the law currently loses to the rule."}, {"id": "extracted_projects_the_method_findings_lowdin_2_13_kraft_pratt_seidenberg", "label": "Kraft, Pratt and Seidenberg (1959)", "file_type": "paper", "source_file": "extracted/projects/the-method/FINDINGS-LOWDIN-2_13.txt", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The founding counterexample: a five-element comparative probability order satisfying every obvious condition and admitting no representing measure."}], "edges": [{"source": "extracted_projects_the_method_findings_lowdin_2_13_chapter_lowdin", "target": "extracted_projects_the_method_findings_lowdin_2_13_lowdin_challenge", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "extracted/projects/the-method/FINDINGS-LOWDIN-2_13.txt", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "extracted_projects_the_method_findings_lowdin_2_13_chapter_lowdin", "target": "extracted_projects_the_method_findings_lowdin_2_13_madelung_wrong_target", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "extracted/projects/the-method/FINDINGS-LOWDIN-2_13.txt", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "extracted_projects_the_method_findings_lowdin_2_13_chapter_lowdin", "target": "extracted_projects_the_method_findings_lowdin_2_13_nu_ordering_functional", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "extracted/projects/the-method/FINDINGS-LOWDIN-2_13.txt", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "extracted_projects_the_method_findings_lowdin_2_13_nu_ordering_functional", "target": "extracted_projects_the_method_findings_lowdin_2_13_nu_deactivation", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "extracted/projects/the-method/FINDINGS-LOWDIN-2_13.txt", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "extracted_projects_the_method_findings_lowdin_2_13_held_out_score", "target": "extracted_projects_the_method_findings_lowdin_2_13_nu_deactivation", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score":